# Karpathy guidelines

Bias toward caution over speed. Trivial one-liners may skip full rigor.

1. **Think before coding** — State assumptions; present interpretations; push back on overkill; stop when confused.
2. **Simplicity first** — Minimum code; no speculative features or abstractions.
3. **Surgical changes** — Touch only what the request requires; match style; clean only your orphans.
4. **Goal-driven execution** — Define verify steps; loop until checks pass.

SIREN hard rules in `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/CONTRACT.md` outrank these.
